<!DOCTYPE CDXML SYSTEM "https://static.chemistry.revvitycloud.com/cdxml/CDXML.dtd" >
<!-- A hand-written two-row, two-step scheme in the form ChemDraw 26 writes one:
     row 1  (I) -i)-> (II)      the arrow a graphic superseded by an arrow object, its step and
                                 the labels' chemical properties given;
     row 2  (II) -ii)-> 4/(III)  its "(II)" placed well below the structure, so only its chemical
                                 property ties it there; no step: the arrow text is found over the
                                 shaft, and the bold "4" is a free text just above the label "(III)".
     (II) carries a nickname node (TEG) with its own fragment, as ChemDraw writes one. -->
